    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 032256\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n256 PM PST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Temperatures will hover within a few degrees of normal through\n  the week, with breezy conditions down the Colorado River Valley\n  later this week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Monday. \n\nShortwave ridging over the area will give way to to a low pressure \nsystem moving through the Great Basin tomorrow, which will \nresult in southerly breezes across the southern Great Basin on \nWednesday. Dry conditions will persist, with precipitation \nchances remaining north of our forecast area. Another system will \ndrop into the region late Thursday into Friday, resulting in an \nuptick in north winds across the region and gusty north winds down\nthe Colorado River Valley. A closed low will develop south of our\nforecast area on Saturday, with high pressure building over Great\nBasin. This will allow for north winds to linger down the \nColorado River Valley on Saturday due to the enhanced north-south \npressure gradient. These winds will result in choppy, 1 to 3 foot \nwaves on Lake Mohave and Lake Havasu Friday and Saturday. \nTemperatures across the region will remain normal-to-slightly \ncooler than normal through the work week, with normal temperatures\nreturning over the weekend into early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain light and generally follow typical daily directional \npatterns through Wednesday morning. By early afternoon, winds \nshift to the northeast and increase to around 8KT, before veering\nto the southwest and becoming light late in the period. Clouds \nwill diminish through this evening, with clear skies expected \nthereafter with VFR conditions prevailing.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds across the\nregion will generally remain between 5-10KT and follow typical \ndaily directional patterns through Wednesday morning. The primary \nexception is the northern Owens Valley/KBIH where up-valley winds \nwith gusts to around 20KT shift to the north after sunset with a \nlull overnight before gusts return late morning. Additionally, \nwesterly winds across the western Mojave Desert/KDAG will develop \ngusts to 20-25KT overnight. Areawide, winds shift to the north and\nnortheast by early Wednesday afternoon, with sustained speeds \ngenerally around 8-10KT. Skies will clear by late evening and VFR \nconditions will prevail.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
